// Inline rich text: the `span` family, and the `richText` node that shows a
// run of it. A component joins the family by naming that tree in its return
// position.
//
// The family is inline and nothing else — emphasis, a link, a piece of code
// inside a sentence — because inline is the part of a document that has no
// other way to be said. A heading is a `text` with a size, a quote is a `vbox`
// with a rule down its left edge, a list is a `vbox` of rows; all three are
// ordinary layout, already implemented on every platform, and a markup
// component for each would be a construct five platforms reimplement to reach
// what `sngl:ui` hands them. A bold word inside a sentence is not: it has to
// live inside one flow of text with the words around it, and a box cannot hold
// it without breaking the line.
//
// So a document is a `vbox` of `richText` runs interleaved with whatever else
// the document holds — a code sample, a table, a chart — and each `richText`
// is one flow. That is also what makes a document extensible: a thing this
// package cannot express is a `ui.node` placed between two runs rather than a
// gap in the vocabulary.
